var/
persona/
persona.md
persona.md.bak-*
memory-okf*/
_task_state/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
ui/node_modules/
# session scratch lives at the ROOT only — an unanchored `_*.py` would also swallow every
# harness/**/__init__.py and harness_tests/_gate.py (it did, once: 2026-08-21)
/_*.py
/_*.log
/_*.err
/_*.out
/_*.ps1
!harness_tests/_gate.py
*.7z
.env

# the session-memory sidecar writes here (.remember/now.md, today-*.md, logs/).
# It ships its OWN nested .gitignore, and relying on a file a tool creates is not a
# guarantee: if it is ever missing, a transcript full of his name and absolute paths
# lands in a repo. Ignored at the root as well, belt and braces (2026-08-23).
.remember/

# state, never source (2026-08-28, external review): a clone that
# mints nexus.db must not commit it — the source repo tracked its own for
# three days after the rule was written.
data/

# THE OPTIONAL NATIVE ENGINE, if you clone it (docs/BACKENDS.md).
# It goes HERE, at engine/, and not beside this tree: serve.py does
# `from engine.launch import launch_daemon`, which resolves relative to the Kairos
# root. A sibling clone refuses politely and then cannot proceed.
# Its own repo tracks it; this tree must not.
/engine/
